PROPOSED, NOT MEASURED (no device here). Two config-only changes for the native iOS build.

1) Unlock ProMotion. Without this key iOS caps CADisplayLink (Reanimated, Skia, RN) at 60 Hz on
   an iPhone 16 Pro, while the system UI runs at 120 Hz.

--- a/app.json
+++ b/app.json
@@ "ios": {
     "infoPlist": {
+      "CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone": true,
       "NSAppTransportSecurity": {

2) Reanimated 4 static feature flags (package.json, read at native build time). With the default
   (false), each animated prop update goes through a ShadowTree commit; the table updates ~139
   per-card gloss/shade layers plus flights every frame. Needs a device A/B (bench `restCost`,
   `throws`) and a check of the gesture-handler Pressable caveat in Reanimated's docs.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@
+  "reanimated": {
+    "staticFeatureFlags": {
+      "IOS_SYNCHRONOUSLY_UPDATE_UI_PROPS": true,
+      "ANDROID_SYNCHRONOUSLY_UPDATE_UI_PROPS": true
+    }
+  },
